{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/pulls/335","id":4424297442,"node_id":"PR_kwDOP42Xbc8AAAABB7Vr4g","html_url":"https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/pull/335","diff_url":"https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/pull/335.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/pull/335.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/335","number":335,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"The non-RTL required contexts pin their gate steps, presence and step lists (#295)","user":{"login":"Mister-M-alt","id":161579364,"node_id":"U_kgDOCaGBZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161579364?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"[A0]\n\n## Status\n\nGREEN — `scripts/ci_events.py` + `docs/testing/CI_WORKFLOWS.md` (2 commits, no workflow edits). ci_events --check OK at **920 contract items** (was 714) across all four workflows unmodified; --selftest PASS at **389 arms** (was 332; +55 lever arms + 2 on-disk duplicate-mapping controls), vacuity control fails 353 of 389 — every substantive arm including all 55 new lever arms; the 2 on-disk duplicate-mapping controls are proven under the stub separately ([R1]). docs/style/toc/paths gates clean; py_compile; git diff --check.\n\n## What is pinned, mirroring the house idioms\n\nThe four steps the [R3]/[R4] rounds on PR #293 proved evadable are held the way the builder/gate/decide steps already are — canonical normalised script, exact key set, refusals for `if`/`shell`/`continue-on-error`/`working-directory`/non-canonical script, each refusal NAMING the step:\n\n- **docs-check**'s ci_events gate step and **docs-check-no-git**'s single step (the `--check || true` substring evasion dies);\n- **wire-accountability**'s gate step;\n- **elaborate**'s scope step, held like the RTL decide step (#209 precedent): key set including its `env` bindings, whole-script equality, and `ci_scope.py --selftest` structurally BEFORE the answer is read.\n\n**Presence**: each gate step exactly once in the id-named job — the [R3]-round-2 stub-job rename and the PyYAML last-wins duplicate-mapping trick both refuse naming the job (the duplicate case proven on real appended duplicates in the on-disk selftest controls).\n\n**Step lists** for all four carriers: count, order, per-step identity, exact key sets, exact `if` values and `with` mappings — the [R4]-round-6 insertion class (a `run:` step writing `BASH_ENV` to `$GITHUB_ENV`, a `$GITHUB_PATH` prepend, any third-party `uses:`) is refused by count/order before its content matters.\n\n## The battery, scripted and kept\n\n19 levers from the issue's evidence, each applied to a scratch copy, each rc 1 with its naming refusal, baseline and restored copies rc 0 (transcript in the lane record): if/continue-on-error/`|| true` ×4 steps, the scope rewrite to `rtl=false`, the dropped scope selftest, the stub rename, the appended duplicate, and the three insertion levers.\n\n## One scope item for this round to adjudicate\n\nThe issue's acceptance table carries a **widened row** (sequence pins on the seven remaining RTL jobs; content pins on non-gate carrier steps) that its own in-scope list does not include and its out-of-scope list (\"The RTL workflows (already held)\") arguably excludes. This lane implements the in-scope list exactly; CI_WORKFLOWS.md item 12 now states the residue honestly as still open. If the round reads the widened row as binding, say so and the lane extends; otherwise the residue becomes the recorded follow-up.\n\n## How to validate\n\n```sh\npython3 scripts/ci_events.py --check      # 920 items, four workflows untouched\npython3 scripts/ci_events.py --selftest   # 389 arms\n```\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- [x] Four steps pinned (keys + canonical script), refusals name the step\n- [x] Presence exactly-once in the id-named job; stub/duplicate evasions refused naming the job\n- [x] Carrier step lists pinned; the insertion class refused\n- [x] One reason-pinned arm per lever per step; vacuity fails them all\n- [x] Policy page states the pins and drops the caveat\n- [ ] The round adjudicates the widened-row scope question\n- [ ] Review positive; hosted green; containment post-merge\n\nRelates to #295 — [R1]'s ruling: the widened acceptance row (RTL job sequence pins, non-gate content pins) binds the ISSUE, not this lane, so #295 stays open on that residue after this merges (it will be reopened deliberately if the branch link auto-closes it).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n","created_at":"2026-09-02T16:18:53Z","updated_at":"2026-09-02T16:54:51Z","closed_at":"2026-09-02T16:54:50Z","merged_at":"2026-09-02T16:54:50Z","merge_commit_sha":"b16cb4702b846de7a1ad3ee99013e9ef23db4560","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/pulls/335/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/pulls/335/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ke